.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-COMPONENT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-component
.Nd add, remove and inspect kldload's optional components after installation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm list
.Nm
.Cm status
.Ar name
.Nm
.Cm install | remove
.Op Fl -now
.Ar name ...
.Nm
.Cm log
.Ar name
.Op Fl f
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A component is a capability that can be added to an installed kldload
machine, or taken away, after the fact:
.Bl -tag -width "zfslab"
.It Li kvm
KVM and libvirt: run virtual machines here.
.It Li k8s
A Kubernetes cluster in virtual machines, with Cilium, Hubble and
MetalLB.
.It Li klab
The multi-distribution test bay: cloud-image goldens and blue/green
clones.
.It Li zfslab
The OpenZFS development lab: goldens with the source and its test suite.
.It Li ai
A local language model and its chat, offline.
.El
.Pp
The installer, first boot, the automatic deployment and the consoles all
add components through this one command, so adding Kubernetes later is
the same as having chosen it at install time.
.Pp
.Cm install
and
.Cm remove
run the work as a system unit,
.Pa kldload-comp- Ns Ar name ,
and return at once: closing the terminal, the console tab or the ssh
session does not stop it.
.Cm log
.Fl f
follows it.
With
.Fl -now
the work runs in the foreground instead, and the exit status says how it
went.
A component that needs another installs that first.
Installing an installed component asserts it again, which is how a
failed or interrupted one is finished.
.Pp
Each component has a state:
.Bl -tag -width "interrupted"
.It Li absent
Not installed.
.It Li installed
Installed through this command, and its own check agrees.
.It Li missing
Recorded as installed, and its check no longer finds it.
.It Li unmanaged
Present, put there by its own tool rather than through this command
\(em a cluster made with
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
goldens made with
.Xr klab 8 .
.It Li running
Being installed or removed now.
.It Li interrupted
Its work stopped part-way: a reboot or a power cut.
Install it again.
.It Li failed
Its install or remove returned an error; the log says what.
.El
.Pp
.Cm list ,
.Cm status
and
.Cm log
need no root; the checks use the system libvirt whoever asks.
.Cm install
and
.Cm remove
need root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm list
Every component with its state, roughly how many minutes it takes, and
what it is; the default.
.It Cm status Ar name
The component's state, one word, for scripts.
.It Cm install Ar name ...
.It Cm remove Ar name ...
Add or take away each component, detached.
.It Fl -now
Run the work here and wait for it.
.It Cm log Ar name Op Fl f
Print the component's work log, or follow it.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_COMPONENT_REG , KLDLOAD_COMPONENT_STATE , KLDLOAD_LOG_DIR
The registry, state and log directories instead of the ones below.
.It Ev LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI
The libvirt the checks ask; default
.Ql qemu:///system .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/lib/kldload/components/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .component
Each component: a summary, an estimate, what it requires, and its install,
remove and status verbs.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/components/ Ns Ar name
Its recorded state.
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/component- Ns Ar name Ns Pa .log
Everything its work printed, every run.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Done; for a detached
.Cm install
or
.Cm remove ,
started.
.It 1
A usage error, an unknown component, no log yet, or
.Cm install
or
.Cm remove
run without root.
.It 2
With
.Fl -now :
a component's work failed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-29.
.Ss What there is (list, status)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-component list
NAME         STATE        APPROX   SUMMARY
ai           absent       ~15m     Local LLM: ollama + chat model, fully offline
k8s          absent       ~25m     Kubernetes cluster in VMs (Cilium eBPF, Hubble, MetalLB)
klab         unmanaged    ~25m     Multi-distro test bay: stock cloud-image goldens + blue/green clones
kvm          unmanaged    ~5m      KVM/libvirt host: run VMs on this machine
zfslab       absent       ~40m     OpenZFS dev lab: golden VMs with the source + upstream test suite
# (exited 0)
$ kldload-component status klab
unmanaged
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
This machine's klab goldens were built with
.Xr klab 8
directly, so klab is
.Ql unmanaged .
.Ss Installing and removing (install, remove, log, --now)
Against a registry made for the purpose, with one component,
.Ql quick ,
whose verbs do nothing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# export KLDLOAD_COMPONENT_REG=/var/tmp/comptest-3443758/reg KLDLOAD_COMPONENT_STATE=/var/tmp/comptest-3443758/state KLDLOAD_LOG_DIR=/var/tmp/comptest-3443758/log
# kldload-component install quick
Running as unit: kldload-comp-quick.service; invocation ID: 28e3ef312c6243919b2005b20c26bec6
install quick: started (detached) — kldload-component log quick -f
# (exited 0)
# kldload-component status quick
installed
# (exited 0)
# kldload-component log quick
\&...
═══ install quick — 2026-09-29T23:55:54-07:00 ═══
installing nothing
OK: install quick
# (exited 0)
# kldload-component remove --now quick
═══ remove quick — 2026-09-29T23:55:57-07:00 ═══
removing nothing
OK: remove quick
# (exited 0)
# kldload-component status quick
absent
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
A component whose install fails:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-component install --now broken
═══ install broken — 2026-09-29T23:56:59-07:00 ═══
fetching nothing
FATAL: install broken failed (rc=3) — see /var/tmp/comptest-f3450047/log/component-broken.log
# (exited 2)
# kldload-component status broken
failed
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss What it refuses
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-component install ai
kldload-component: install must run as root (list, status and log do not)
# (exited 1)
# kldload-component install nosuch
kldload-component: unknown component 'nosuch'
  known: quick
# (exited 1)
# kldload-component status
usage: kldload-component status <name>
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "FATAL: VERB NAME failed (rc=N) \(em see LOG"
The component's work returned
.Ar N ;
its log has the rest.
.It "kldload-component: NAME is already running \(em 'log NAME -f' to watch"
An install or remove of it is still going; nothing new was started.
.It "kldload-component: 'NAME' has no VERB verb"
The component cannot be removed, or installed, this way.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kld 1 ,
.Xr systemd-run 1 ,
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8
.Sh HISTORY
Components replaced seven environment variables that asked for the same
work in different words, and tick boxes that could be chosen only at
install time.
The work was detached after a 40-minute golden build died with the
console tab that started it (2026-08-14).
.Ql unmanaged
dates from 2026-09-01, when the table said
.Ql absent
for Kubernetes, klab and KVM on a machine running all three, installed by
their own tools.
.Pp
On 2026-09-29, writing this page:
run as a user, the checks asked the user's own, empty, libvirt, and
.Cm install
waited 25 seconds on an authentication prompt nobody could see before it
failed; and
.Cm status
printed the recorded state while
.Cm list
printed the reconciled one, so a script and the table disagreed.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The exit statuses are this tool's own: a usage error is 1, not 2, and 2 is
a failed component.
.Pp
A detached
.Cm install
exits 0 when the work has started, not when it has finished; watch
.Cm status
or the log.
